    kgjobs:sourceOccurrence <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/live/occurrence/arbeitnow-internship-go-to-market-engineering-ai-automation-berlin-481074/1> ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "internship-go-to-market-engineering-ai-automation-berlin-481074" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-09-08"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Dein Impact autarc is building the operating system for energy installers across Europe. As we scale, we want our Go-to-Market organization to operate with the same level of automation, data quality, and product thinking as our engineering organization. In this Internship, you will work on the technical infrastructure behind our revenue engine. You will work directly with our Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, Operations, and Product teams to identify bottlenecks, build internal tools, automate workflows, connect systems, and deploy AI where it creates measurable commercial impact. Role description What You’ll Do Work on our GTM operating system Build the systems powering our entire customer lifecycle – from first lead to closed customer and expansion. Build internal applications and workflows that help SDRs, Account Executives, Customer Success Managers, and leadership make better decisions and execute faster. Turn fragmented processes into scalable systems. Automate the revenue engine Identify repetitive or inefficient workflows across Sales, Marketing, and Customer Success and automate them. Build automations for areas such as lead enrichment, routing, qualification, follow-ups, pipeline management, customer onboarding, and retention. Connect our GTM stack and ensure information moves reliably between systems. Integrate AI into real workflows Move AI beyond prototypes. Build AI-powered workflows that help us qualify and prioritize leads, analyze calls and customer interactions, identify opportunities and risks, generate insights, and automate operational work. Experiment rapidly with new models and tools and turn successful experiments into reliable internal products. Build, don’t just recommend You will personally implement what you design. Depending on the problem, that might mean writing Python or TypeScript, building an n8n workflow, connecting an API, querying a database, prototyping an internal application, or working with our engineers on a deeper integration. You should be comfortable moving between commercial conversations and technical implementation. Drive measurable commercial impact Technology is a means, not the outcome. Your work should ultimately help us generate more pipeline, increase conversion, shorten sales cycles, improve retention, or allow our GTM organization to scale without adding unnecessary complexity. You will work closely with GTM leadership to identify the highest-leverage problems and own them from idea to measurable result. Requirements You are a builder. When you see a broken process, your instinct is to understand it and build something better. You have strong technical skills and have worked in Python and/or TypeScript You have hands-on experience building automations and integrations using tools such as n8n and APIs You are comfortable working with databases, APIs, webhooks, and data pipelines You are interested in Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, and the systems behind how SAAS companies create revenue You can translate an ambiguous business problem into a technical solution without needing a detailed specification You move fast, iterate, and are comfortable shipping a first version before everything is perfect You are fluent in English. German or another European language is a plus Bonus Points You have first experience in a dynamic start-up environment and have worked on technical solutions Tools like HubSpot, Aircall, Stripe, Intercom, PostHog, or similar platforms are not entirely new for you Ideally you have worked on or build internal tools, AI agents, lead-scoring systems, enrichment pipelines, or automated outbound workflows. You have worked in an early-stage or high-growth startup where speed and ownership mattered more than clearly defined responsibilities. Was wir bieten An internship with direct influence on how autarc scales its commercial organization. The opportunity to build GTM infrastructure and directly collaborate with our founders and GTM leadership. A strong engineering and product culture combined with an ambitious commercial organization. A beautiful office in Berlin and a team that values working together in person. MacBook and everything else you need to do your best work. Most importantly: a role where your output can directly influence how quickly autarc grows Unsere Werte Why autarc? autarc is building the AI operating system for energy installers. Our platform helps installers manage the entire workflow around renewable energy projects – from lead and site assessment to technical planning, offers, documentation, installation, and ongoing operations. We already serve more than 2,000 businesses and are expanding our platform across Europe. As our Go-to-Market Engineer, you won’t inherit a finished system. You will help design the next generation of our commercial infrastructure. You will work directly with leadership, have access to the entire GTM organization, and be able to ship solutions that are used by the team immediately. No endless strategy decks. No six-month implementation projects. Find the bottleneck. Build the solution. Measure whether it worked. Improve it. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full time, Permanent, Student" ;
