    kgjobs:reconciliationReason "no reviewed first-party candidate" ;
    kgjobs:sourceOccurrence <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/live/occurrence/arbeitnow-product-owner-all-genders-management-suite-tribe-augsburg-488192/1> ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "product-owner-all-genders-management-suite-tribe-augsburg-488192" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Welcome to baramundi! “Where security, automation and centralized control come together, modern endpoint management begins.” Do you want to actively shape modern UEM solutions, translate technical complexity into clear product decisions and create real value for IT administrators together with strong development teams? Then become part of our Management Suite Tribe and help drive the further development of our primarily on-premise Unified Endpoint Management solution as a Product Owner. At baramundi, we develop software solutions that enable companies to centrally manage, secure and automate their endpoints. As a Product Owner, you work closely with development, Product Management, Support, Consulting and our customers in an agile, interdisciplinary environment. Your goal: to translate product requirements into valuable, prioritized and actionable features. Do what you do best: DRIVE PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT IN THE MANAGEMENT SUITE TRIBE You take content responsibility for two development squads and, together with them, further develop key product areas of the baramundi Management Suite, primarily in Windows Endpoint Management – from fundamental client-server communication to compliance and defense management, Windows OS installation, co-management and Windows Update Management. You are part of the Product Owner Chapter and work closely within the leadership trio of Chapter Lead, Scrum Master and Product Owner. TRANSLATE REQUIREMENTS INTO CLEAR PRODUCT INCREMENTS You understand technical and functional complexity, formulate features and product backlog items precisely and ensure clear, testable acceptance criteria. You prioritize the product backlog based on customer value, effort, dependencies and stakeholder input. DELIVER WITH YOUR TEAMS You are the primary contact person for content-related and product-related questions from your development teams, make progress transparent and ensure that your squads can work in a focused, informed and empowered way. At the same time, you balance maintenance, quality and new features. BE THE BRIDGE BETWEEN PRODUCT, DEVELOPMENT AND STAKEHOLDERS You work closely with Product Management, Support, Consulting, customers as well as internal and external development partners, actively gather feedback and translate requirements into concrete development steps. In doing so, you represent product value just as clearly as the perspective of your teams. COORDINATE EXTERNAL PROJECTS AND DEVELOPMENT SERVICES You coordinate external teams and projects from a content perspective, ensure clear requirements, transparent alignment and reliable integration into product development. USE AI MEANINGFULLY IN YOUR PRODUCT OWNER ROUTINE You use AI tools in a reflective and pragmatic way – for example when creating features and PBIs, structuring requirements or developing quick prototypes for stakeholder feedback. What we appreciate about you: Several years of experience as a Product Owner or in a comparable role with product responsibility in an agile software development environment. Experience in providing content leadership for multiple development teams as well as integrating and coordinating external projects or developers. Confidence working with Scrum, Kanban and backlog tools – ideally Azure DevOps – as well as experience in scaled agile ways of working. Solid knowledge of or strong interest in Unified Endpoint Management, Client Lifecycle Management and Windows-based IT infrastructures. Ability to quickly understand technical complexity and translate it into clear, prioritizable requirements. Analytical, data-based decision-making and a high standard of quality. Strong communication skills in German and English and enjoyment in working with different stakeholders. Ability to provide content leadership at eye level, create orientation and foster open, transparent exchange within the team. Bonus: background in IT administration, practical knowledge of software development, experience with the Azure technology stack or touchpoints with Linux, macOS, Android or iOS. Meet us! 10 reasons to choose baramundi! #1 ARRIVE IN PEACE Our all-inclusive package makes starting particularly easy. Your personal onboarding buddy will show you everything: from the welcome breakfast to the fully equipped workplace. #2 FEEL AT HOME Coffee, fruit, and drinks are free. We take care of your mail and packages. Once a month, all baramundians meet during work hours for pizza and chatting. Just because. #3 EXPERIENCE VALUE AND APPRECIATION We believe in values and live them: togetherness and trust. Courage, enthusiasm, and competence. Our communication culture is open and honest. Just like the regular team feedback sessions. #4 GET REWARDED You will also feel our appreciation. Success bonuses are as natural as Christmas bonuses, company pension plans, and team events. #5 ENJOY LIFE Work time is life time. That’s why you can organize it individually with us. With flexible working hours in full or part-time, home office, and even sabbatical options. #6 STAY HEALTHY We want you to feel good. That’s why we have ergonomic furniture and organize health days, massages, yoga, and running groups. #7 DEVELOP FURTHER Your personal and professional advancement is important to us. We pay for training and coaching during working hours. Even two-year work stays at our branch in the USA are possible. #8 WORK AT EYE LEVEL We are all on a first-name basis, from apprentices to management. We don’t have complicated hierarchies. #9 YOUR FAMILY IS IMPORTANT TO US Family means being there, caring, and supporting each other. We do this with daycare subsidies and holiday care, as well as at our family summer festival. #10 MAKE US EVEN BETTER We want to be a great place and employer. For that, we need honest feedback. Contact us! Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Experienced, Full time, Permanent" ;
