    schema:description "<div class=\"content-intro\"><p><strong>Welcome to Planet. We believe in using space to help life on Earth.</strong></p> <p>Planet designs, builds, and operates the largest constellation of imaging satellites in history. This constellation delivers an unprecedented dataset of empirical information via a revolutionary cloud-based platform to authoritative figures in commercial, environmental, and humanitarian sectors. We are both a space company and data company all rolled into one.</p> <p>Customers and users across the globe use Planet's data to develop new technologies, drive revenue, power research, and solve our world’s toughest obstacles.</p> <p>As we control every component of hardware design, manufacturing, data processing, and software engineering, our office is a truly inspiring mix of experts from a variety of domains.</p> <p>We have a people-centric approach toward culture and community and we strive to iterate in a way that puts our team members first and prepares our company for growth. Join Planet and be a part of our mission to change the way people see the world.</p> <p>Planet is a global company with employees working remotely world wide and joining us from offices in San Francisco, Washington DC, Germany, Austria, Slovenia, and The Netherlands.</p></div><p><strong>About the Role:&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p> <p>The <strong>Director of Pre-Sales, Global Defence &amp; Intelligence (D&amp;I)</strong> will be responsible for leading Pre-Sales Solution Architects worldwide. This leader will deliver excellence in technical sales, account strategy, relationship building, and solution architecting tailored specifically to national security, Defence &amp; Intelligence institutions.</p> <p>The mission of Pre-Sales is to provide trusted technical advice, enabling global defence customers to leverage Earth Observation data and geospatial intelligence to support critical military operations, decision-making, and strategic outcomes.</p> <p>The ideal candidate is an accomplished people manager, a geospatial expert with strong commercial acumen, and possesses over 10 years of experience in Defence &amp; Intelligence. You possess a deep understanding of government defense customers, complex procurement frameworks, and military command structures.</p> <p>This is a visible, strategic, and highly influential global role, partnering closely with internal D&amp;I Sales teams, Space Systems, Product Engineering, and trusted defense partner ecosystems to secure complex, large-scale government contracts.</p> <p>This is a full-time, remote position based in the UK or Germany. If located near an office, you are expected to work from that office 3 days per week.</p> <p><strong>Impact You’ll Own:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Create the conditions for high performance; recruit, coach, and develop a global team of specialized D&amp;I Pre-Sales Solution Architects.</li> <li>Support global D&amp;I sales teams and partner ecosystems by providing world-class technical sales capability to win new defense programs and expand existing accounts.</li> <li>Apply deep expertise in remote sensing, imagery analytics, and complex data architecture to design solutions supporting Military Operations, Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance (ISR) workflows.</li> <li>Lead high-impact customer engagements, workshops, pilots, and technical demonstrations tailored to defense commanders, intelligence analysts, and procurement officers.</li> <li>Collaborate closely with Global Professional Services, Program Management and Customer Success to conduct rigorous technical assessments, ensuring flawless execution from validation to operational delivery.</li> <li>Feed insights, security requirements, and intelligence use cases directly back to Product and Marketing to shape the product roadmap.</li> <li>Serve as a core member of the Global Pre-Sales &amp; Services leadership team, shaping overarching department strategy and driving execution.</li> </ul> <p><strong>What You Bring:</strong></p> <ul> <li>8+ years of relevant work experience and 6+ years of supervisory or leadership experience managing and scaling technical sales (Pre-Sales / Solution Architecture) teams.</li> <li>8+ years of professional experience in a Defence &amp; Intelligence environment.</li> <li>Active Security Clearance (or eligibility to hold suitable clearance for engaging all levels of Military Command).</li> <li>Solid grasp of military planning, intelligence workflows, and how commercial Earth Observation (EO) data integrates into defense decision-making.</li> <li>Experience navigating complex government sales cycles, RFP/RFI processes, and defense contracting frameworks.</li> <li>Fluency in geospatial system architectures, cloud environments/secure deployments, API integrations, and complex data pipelines.</li> <li>Ability to engage senior defense executives, military leaders, and procurement authorities, translating technical complexity into strategic value.</li> <li>Excellent communication, organizational, and leadership skills with a track record of building resilient, high-trust teams.</li> </ul> <p><strong>What Makes You Stand Out:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Military / Veteran Experience: Former active Armed Forces Reserve or veteran intelligence professional.</li> <li>Experience working with Sales Qualification frameworks and methodologies e.g., Challenger Sales, MEDDPICC.</li> <li>Understanding of AI-Driven Geospatial Innovation: Conversant in modern AI/ML capabilities (e.g., automated feature extraction, change detection, foundation models) and skilled at leveraging AI to demonstrate high-value intelligence outcomes to defense customers—moving beyond raw imagery to automated, actionable insights.&nbsp;</li> <li>Experience co-selling and architecting solutions alongside major defense prime contractors, system integrators, and international allies.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Application Deadline:</strong></p> <p>November 30, 2026 at 11:59p PT</p> <p><strong>Benefits While Working at Planet:</strong></p> <p><em>These offerings are dependent on employment type and geographical location, based upon applicable law or company policy.</em></p> <ul> <li>Paid time off including vacation, holidays and company-wide days off&nbsp;</li> <li>Employee Wellness Program&nbsp;</li> <li>Home Office Reimbursement</li> <li>Monthly Phone and Internet Reimbursement</li> <li>Tuition Reimbursement and access to LinkedIn Learning</li> <li>Equity&nbsp;</li> <li>Volunteering Paid Time Off</li> </ul> <p><strong>Compensation:</strong></p> <p>The expected starting gross salary range for this role is listed below. Individual placement within this range is determined objectively based on gender-neutral criteria such as your skills, qualifications, and professional experience. This position may also be eligible for discretionary bonuses, commission, and/or equity.</p> <div id=\"message-list_1788369991.807479\"> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div>In addition to the salary range listed below, this role is also eligible to receive commission.</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <h6><span style=\"font-weight: 300; font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;\">#LI-REMOTE</span></h6><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">Germany Salary Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>€91.070</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>€113.820 EUR</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><strong>San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance<br></strong>Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.<strong><br></strong></p> <p><strong>Why we care so much about Belonging.&nbsp;<br></strong>We’re dedicated to helping the whole Planet, and to do that we must strive to represent all of it within each of our offices and on all of our teams. That’s why Planet is guided by an ultimate north star of Belonging—dreaming big as we approach our ongoing work.&nbsp; If this job intrigues you, but you’re thinking you might not have all the qualifications, please... do apply!&nbsp; At Planet, we are looking for well-rounded people from around the world who can contribute to more ways than just what is listed in this job description.&nbsp; We don’t just fill positions, we aspire to fulfill people’s careers, most excited about folks who are motivated by our underlying humanitarian efforts.&nbsp; We are a few orbits around the sun before we get to where we want to be, so we hope you’re excited to come along for the ride.&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>EEO statement: <br></strong>Planet is committed to building a community where everyone belongs and we invite people from all backgrounds to apply. Planet is an equal opportunity employer, and committed to providing employment opportunities regardless of race, religious creed, color, national origin, ancestry, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, childbirth and breastfeeding, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other protected classification, in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws. <a href=\"https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf\">Know Your Rights.</a></p> <p><strong>Accommodations:&nbsp;<br></strong>Planet is an inclusive community and we know that everyone has their own needs. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation during the hiring process, please reach out to ----- or contact your recruiter with your request. Your message will be confidential and we will be happy to assist you.</p> <p><strong>Privacy Policy</strong>: By clicking \"Apply Now\" at the top of this job posting, I acknowledge that I have read the <a href=\"https://www.planet.com/privacy/#california\">Planet Data Privacy Notice for California Staff Members and Applicants</a>, and hereby consent to the collection, processing, use, and storage of my personal information as described therein.</p> <p><strong>Privacy Policy (European Applicants):</strong> By clicking \"Apply Now\" at the top of this job posting, I acknowledge that I have read the <a href=\"https://www.planet.com/privacy/\">Candidate Privacy Notice GDPR Planet Labs Europe</a>, and hereby consent to the collection, processing, use, and storage of my personal information as described therein.</p> <p><strong>AI in Our Interviewing Process</strong>: Planet is committed to providing an exceptional interview experience for all candidates. We currently use <a href=\"https://www.metaview.ai/\" target=\"_blank\">Metaview</a> to better focus on candidates and less on trying to capture notes. As such, with the candidate's consent, select interviews may be recorded and include a \"Planet AI Notetaker\" for transcription and summarization purposes. Should an interview involve use of AI interview technologies, the candidate will receive notification and have the ability to opt out both in advance and/or real-time. Opting out will not affect one's candidacy.</p> <p><strong>Candidate AI Policy</strong>: Planet embraces Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools, and we encourage its responsible use. We understand that candidates may use various resources, including AI tools, to <em>prepare</em> for interviews and assessments. However, <em>during any live interview stage or when actively completing assessments for this position, the use of AI tools—e.g. Large Language Models (LLMs), deep fake technology, etc.—is strictly prohibited unless explicitly prompted by an interviewer or assessment instructions</em>. If you are unsure about acceptable use, please contact your recruiter for clarification. If an AI tool or similar technology is desired as an accommodation, please contact ----- with your request for assistance. Your message will be confidential, and we will be happy to assist you. Violation of this policy may result in disqualification of your application.</p></div> Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
