easured weekly on activity and demos held. What will you be doing? 😎 Work inbound leads within SLA (minutes, not hours) and convert them to booked demos. Build and execute outbound sequences against target retailer lists; personalise at speed, not at leisure. Qualify hard: right buyer type, purchase volume, intent, timeline. Kill bad leads quickly. Book, confirm, and protect the demo — reduce no-shows with reminders and pre-demo touches. Keep the CRM immaculate: every touch logged, every lead dispositioned, pipeline data trustworthy. Feed learnings back: objections heard, messaging that lands, segments that convert. What do we need from you? 💪 1–3 years in a SaaS or tech-sales SDR/BDR role with a transactional, high-volume motion — short cycles, big numbers, daily intensity. A killer on the phone and crisp in writing; comfortable with 60–80+ meaningful touches a day. Process-driven: you live in cadences and CRM hygiene rather than fighting them. Coachable and resilient — you treat \"no\" as data and keep the energy up on day 20 of the month, not just day 1. Native or professional proficiency in English and German is required for this role. Jewellery knowledge not required; hunger and rigour are. Our culture and what we offer 😉 At Nivoda, we believe that employees today want to evolve in a collaborative, high-growth environment where they can demonstrate their abilities and thrive both professionally and personally. We work to create a culture of empowerment, continuous learning, and growth where everyone can bring their expertise, own projects, and easily measure their impact. Dynamic working environment in a rapidly growing company. Enjoy a pleasant, low-hierarchy work environment. Engage in intellectually challenging work that contributes significantly to Nivoda's success and scalability. Our current benefits 🕰️ Flexible working hours and a vibrant company culture 💻 Remote work 🧠 Plenty of opportunities for growth and learning 🏖️ Unlimited holiday allowance 🚀 Chance to join and contribute to a company during its exponential expansion phase Equal Opportunity Nivoda is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to promoting diversity. We don't discriminate on the basis of race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status or disability status. Even if it seems you don't meet 100% of our musts - don't let it stop you. We are all about finding the best talent out there! Skills can be learned, and embracing diversity is invaluable. Please note: Our Talent Acquisition Team is international. We kindly ask you to submit your CV and application in English so that it can be reviewed correctly. Not quite the right fit? If after reading this job description you believe this is not the best fit for you, we'd encourage you to join our Nivoda Talent Pool so we can keep you in mind as new roles open up. Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
