    schema:description "Company Description We’re Checkout.com. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started. About the team Acquiring is a foundational pillar at Checkout.com. It powers how merchants accept payments and includes the Dashboard experiences that help them understand and manage payment performance. The team also creates reusable patterns and platform capabilities that help other product teams integrate into a consistent Dashboard experience. You’ll join a Design organisation of more than 30 specialists across Product Design, Research, Content, and Technical Writing. The role As a Senior Product Designer, you’ll bring strong interaction and visual design craft to complex B2B software. You’ll work at the centre of the Acquiring Dashboard, shaping the foundations that connect products across Checkout and make payment data easier to understand and act on. This is a hands-on role with real ownership, established foundations to build on, and the opportunity to help level up the experience as we expand into mobile-first products. What you’ll do Own end-to-end design for complex Dashboard experiences in Acquiring, from early concepts through to shipped product, partnering closely with Product and Engineering. Design scalable wrappers, patterns, and platform foundations that help teams across Checkout integrate experiences into the central Dashboard. Lead design for payment analytics, charting, and core payment pages, translating complex payment information into clear, useful actions. Shape platform-wide AI-assisted and conversational experiences, while contributing to the evolution of mobile-first experiences. What success looks like Acquiring Dashboard experiences, including payment pages and analytics, ship with clear flows, strong usability, and a consistently high level of interaction and visual craft. Reusable patterns and platform foundations help other product teams deliver coherent experiences across Dashboard. Your work helps establish the next generation of Acquiring experiences across desktop, mobile, and AI-enabled product surfaces. What you’ll bring A portfolio showing shipped, complex desktop web experiences in B2B SaaS, fintech, payments, or another regulated product environment. Strong interaction and visual design craft, from information architecture and user flows through to polished interfaces and prototypes. A track record of owning complex features end to end, making clear decisions, and staying accountable for outcomes. Experience partnering closely with Product and Engineering in an iterative product development environment. Active curiosity about AI, with evidence of using AI tools in your day-to-day design workflow. Confidence working with established design systems and reusable patterns, and extending them to solve new product problems. Nice to have Experience designing data-dense dashboards, charts, analytics, or other data visualisation experiences. Experience designing mobile product interfaces. Experience with merchant-facing payment products or operational tools in a regulated environment. Additional Information Bring all of you to work We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one. Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands. We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here. It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable. Life at Checkout.com We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection. Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our Careers Page to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us. For a closer look at daily life at Checkout.com, follow us on LinkedIn and Instagram Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
