    schema:description "Short description Join Septeo CNEE and support challenging client projects in the insolvency industry from the initial requirements gathering through to successful implementation. You’ll combine technical expertise with consulting skills to develop customized solutions for complex business processes. Rather than working on a standard product or processing tickets, you’ll collaborate with our clients to design customized workflows, migrations, and integrations that deliver direct, practical value. If you enjoy taking on responsibility, contributing to technical development, and interacting with clients, we look forward to receiving your application. This role is available throughout Germany. Since interacting with clients and the team is a key part of the position, we expect you to be present at our Karlsruhe office on a regular basis and to attend occasional on-site client meetings. Your mission Design and development of custom extensions, interfaces, workflows, and integrations based on C#/.NET, VBA, and XML Further development and maintenance of an Access-based business application and the underlying MS SQL Server database structures Integration and development of digital case management solutions (eIP, e2A), the Electronic Court and Administrative Mailbox (EGVP), and the integration of electronic signatures Development of pragmatic and sustainable solutions for complex business and technical requirements Consulting and technical support for clients in the digitization and optimization of business processes in the insolvency sector Technical coordination with clients and collaboration with specialized departments within the judiciary Preparation of technical documentation and ensuring proper version control using Git Your profile Several years of work experience in software development or technical consulting in a project-oriented environment In-depth knowledge of C#/.NET, MS Access, MS SQL Server, VBA, and ideally modern web technologies such as Angular, React, or Blazor Experience in analyzing business requirements as well as designing, implementing, and deploying custom software solutions, integrations, and migrations Experience working with electronic signatures and, ideally, electronic legal transactions (e.g., EGVP) or comparable regulated environments A strong understanding of business processes, as well as a passion for providing technical consulting and collaborating with clients A structured, independent, and solution-oriented approach to work, combined with strong communication and teamwork skills Excellent English and German language skills Application process Digital Get-to-Know-You Session During a brief conversation with our recruiters, we’ll discuss our mutual expectations. Technical Interview Next, you’ll get to know the department and gain deeper insights into our projects, technologies, and way of working. Introduction day in Karlsruhe Finally, you’ll visit our headquarters in Karlsruhe. You’ll meet the team, gain insights into real client projects, and get an authentic sense of how we collaborate and work. Benefits Our full range of benefits and perks is explained as part of our recruiting process, but you can already get a good overview on our careers page: https://www.stp.one/en/careers As a European company, our benefits vary by country, but some benefits apply to all employees: Annual training budget and defined career paths Employee referral bonus Mobility: e.g., bike leasing, public transportation subsidies Workation: up to 30 days per year within the EU Screen work glasses Tax-free benefits Events & company parties (summer party, annual kick-off, etc.) Flexible work models (hybrid, remote work, part-time, etc.) English courses for all levels Contact details If you have any questions, please feel free to contact our recruiter! Isabel Ostwald E-Mail: Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
